
1. Setup html2text program to get text without html tags:

```bash
sudo dnf install html2text
```

2. Download a text from this URL link https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/6527/pg6527.txt,
 use curl to save it in a file called linux.txt, 
pipe the result into html2text, use grep to search for debian (case insensitive), 
 and redirect the output into a new file called debian.txt:

```bash
curl -s https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/6527/pg6527.txt | html2text > linux.txt | grep -i debian > debian.txt
```

3. Search for "GNU" and count the number of lines where GNU occur:

```bash
grep -n GNU linux.txt
```

4. Count the number of times the word "server" (case insensitive) appear:

```bash
grep -ci server linux.txt
```

or 

```bash
journalctl | grep -i server | wc -l
```

5. Count the number of times the line starts with the word "server" (case insensitive):

```bash
grep -in ^server linux.txt
```

6. Locate .conf files with hardware in it:

```bash
locate "*.conf" | grep hardware
```

7. Find all pdf files in the system that include the name "secret":

```bash
find / -name "*.pdf" | grep secret
```

8. Because previous commands have lots od permission denied, 
sort out the approved results and redirect the denied results to the void:
 
```bash
find / -name "*.pdf* 2>/dev/null | grep secret
```
